# Key Takeaways

- CI focuses on building and testing applications.
- CD focuses on deployment.
- OpenShift supports Docker, Source-to-Image and Binary build strategies.
- Docker Strategy provides maximum flexibility and is preferred for enterprise applications.
- Build Pods are temporary and exist only during image creation.
- ImageStreams manage image versions and deployment triggers.
- Helm simplifies deployment of multiple Kubernetes resources.
- Enterprise CI/CD pipelines automate the journey from source code to running Pods.
